<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Sacred War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">356–346 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Sacred War of 356–346 BCE was fought between the Phocians, who seized the sanctuary of Delphi, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delphic-amphictyony">Delphic Amphictyony</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a>, the Thessalians and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locrians">Locrians</a>. The Phocians paid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> with the temple treasures. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a> ended the war in 346 BCE, gaining a seat on the Amphictyonic Council and influence in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</p></div>
